WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:01.172
(playful music)

00:00:01.172 --> 00:00:02.630
- [Narrator] This is Musetta.

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:04.350
She's a common squirrel monkey,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.543
but there's nothing common about her.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.791
Squirrel monkeys are from the rainforests

00:00:14.791 --> 00:00:17.260
of the Amazon Basin.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.090
Their fur can range from olive
green to yellow in color.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.330
They have long tails,
which help them balance

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.370
on canopy branches, and they subsist

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.500
on a diet of fruit and insects.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.180
They communicate by using up
to 30 different vocal calls

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.030
and can be quite loud
when they get alarmed.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.240
Although they are labeled least concern

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.390
on the Endangered Species List,

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.630
they are made vulnerable by
the increasing deforestation

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.360
of their natural habitat.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.163
This is the squirrel monkey.

00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:55.291
(bright tones)

